{"conjecture": "Software systems accumulate 'latent coupling'—implicit dependencies between modules that are never declared in interfaces but are created every time a developer relies on an undocumented side-effect, timing assumption, or data format invariant. Because tests and reviews only validate explicit contracts, this latent coupling grows invisibly until modifying any single component risks violating an unseen constraint, causing the system's true dependency graph to become a rigid, interconnected web that resists change."}
